{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-207192-r4518711","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Brioche Stuffing","sourcePageId":207192,"sourceRevision":"4518711","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:33:23Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Brioche%20Stuffing&oldid=4518711","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:45.135Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Holiday recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for stuffing and dressing","Category:Recipes using apple","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using walnut","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"60f3ae982240b811985953d647e38d175d3f1ac2141b4e9d701ec9cf8a6e214b","sourceWikitext":"{{recipe summary\n| category    = Stuffing recipes\n| servings    = \n| time        = 65 minutes\n| difficulty  = 2\n| image       = \n| energy      = \n| note        = \n}}\n{{recipe}}  \n\n'''Brioche bread''' is a slightly sweetened yeast bread, often used in stuffing applications.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] brioche [[Cookbook:Bread|bread]], coarsely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* ½ cup shelled [[Cookbook:Walnut|walnuts]], finely chopped\n* ¼ cup dried [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]], coarsely chopped\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]], to taste\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]], to taste\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* ¼ cup unsalted [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], cut into small cubes\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Onion|red onion]]\n* 2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], smashed and [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] dried rubbed [[Cookbook:Sage|sage]]\n* ¼ cup diced [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine all ingredients in a deep roasting pan. Press into a loose, flat layer.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] in a 375 °F (190 °C) [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] for 25 minutes.\n#Raise temperature to 425 °F (220 °C), and bake for 10 minutes. Serve immediately.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using walnut]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Holiday recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stuffing and dressing]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Brioche Stuffing","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups brioche bread, coarsely chopped","sourceText":"2 cups brioche bread, coarsely chopped","amountText":"2 cups brioche bread, coarsely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup shelled walnuts, finely chopped","sourceText":"½ cup shelled walnuts, finely chopped","amountText":"½ cup shelled walnuts, finely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¼ cup dried apples